# Copy to .env.local and fill in what you have. Everything here is optional:
# without any of it the app runs, and the Connect screen offers the file route
# (an exported .ics) instead of a sign-in.
#
# .env.local is gitignored. Nothing in here is a secret in the usual sense —
# an OAuth client ID for a public client is meant to be visible — but a client
# ID is still tied to whoever registered it, so keep it out of commits.

# Microsoft 365 — portal.azure.com → App registrations → new registration.
# Platform: Single-page application. Redirect URI: http://localhost:5199
VITE_MS_CLIENT_ID=

# Google — console.cloud.google.com → APIs & Services → Credentials →
# OAuth client ID → Web application. Authorised origin and redirect:
# http://localhost:5199
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Zoom — marketplace.zoom.us → Develop → Build App → General App, PKCE enabled.
# Zoom's API sends no CORS headers, so this one needs the proxy below.
VITE_ZOOM_CLIENT_ID=

# Apple — developer.apple.com → Identifiers → Services ID (needs a paid
# account). Apple refuses http://localhost as a redirect, so this one only
# completes behind an https address. The client secret is a JWT the dev server
# signs; these four are read by vite.config.ts and never reach the browser.
VITE_APPLE_CLIENT_ID=
APPLE_TEAM_ID=
APPLE_KEY_ID=
APPLE_SERVICES_ID=
APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY=./AuthKey_XXXXXXXX.p8

# You do not need any of the above to bring an iCloud calendar in. Publish it
# from the Calendar app (share a calendar → Public Calendar) and paste the
# webcal link into the Connect screen.

# The dev server forwards token exchanges and Zoom's API (see vite.config.ts).
# Leave it unset to talk to Microsoft and Google directly, which they allow for
# a registered single-page app.
VITE_OAUTH_PROXY=/oauth

# Supabase — accounts and cross-device sync. Create a project at supabase.com,
# then Project Settings → API. Only the publishable (anon) key belongs here:
# it is meant to be public, and security comes from the row-level policies in
# supabase/schema.sql, not from hiding it.
#
# The secret / service key must NEVER go in this file or any build variable —
# it bypasses row-level security entirely. The app has no use for it.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_KEY=
